================================================================================
T-CONNECT OTT LESOTHO M10 VOUCHER TEST GUIDE (VERIFIED HASH & ENDPOINT)
================================================================================

ROOT CAUSE OF YOUR EARLIER HTTP 401:
1. `/api/v1/CheckVoucher` is the Reseller endpoint. For a Merchant account like
   `TCONNECTLES1`, the check endpoint is `/api/v1/CheckRemitVoucher` and the
   redemption endpoint is `/api/v1/RemitVoucher`.
2. In OTT Lesotho's .NET API, `API_KEY` goes FIRST in the SHA-256 hash, followed
   by the parameters in alphabetical order:
   - For CheckRemitVoucher: `SHA256(apiKey + uniqueReference)`
   - For RemitVoucher:      `SHA256(apiKey + amount + mobile + pin + uniqueReference + vendorID)`

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. SAFE PRE-CHECK (RETURNS HTTP 201 WITHOUT BURNING YOUR VOUCHER)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Copy and paste this on your VPS (`rphooko@vmi3475343:~$`) to verify your
`TCONNECTLES1` credentials + `API_KEY` immediately:

API_KEY="4323e6fa-09b2-4eaa-9b73-f275dad58787"
OTT_USER="TCONNECTLES1"
OTT_PASS='3*68pF&24*'
REF="CHK$(date +%s)"
HASH=$(printf "%s%s" "$API_KEY" "$REF" | sha256sum | awk '{print $1}')

curl -i -X POST "https://api.ottlesotho.com/api/v1/CheckRemitVoucher" \
  -H "Authorization: Basic $(printf '%s:%s' "$OTT_USER" "$OTT_PASS" | base64 -w 0)" \
  -F "uniqueReference=${REF}" \
  -F "hash=${HASH}"

